1	2026-08-06 00:22:04.375916	2026-08-06 00:22:04.375923	\N	\N	Bible Foundations	f	\N	0	Learn why the Bible is God's inspired Word, how it was given to humanity, and why it serves as the foundation for Christian faith and practice.	\N	/Users/macbook/uploads/ec67346d-0851-4724-b595-40b5380d6a39_genzura1.3.jpeg	300	2026-08-05	3	The Bible: God's Word and Authority	3	Lesson 1: The Bible – God's Word and Authority\r\nIntroduction\r\nThe Bible is the foundation of the Christian faith. It reveals who God is, explains His plan for humanity, teaches us how to live, and provides guidance for every aspect of life. Christians believe that the Bible is not merely a collection of human writings but the inspired Word of God given through human authors under the guidance of the Holy Spirit.\r\nStudying the Bible helps us understand God's character, His love for humanity, and His plan of salvation through Jesus Christ. It is the primary source of truth and the standard by which Christians evaluate beliefs and practices.\r\n\r\nLearning Objectives\r\nBy the end of this lesson, learners should be able to:\r\n* Understand what the Bible is and why it is important.\r\n* Explain how the Bible was inspired by God.\r\n* Identify the two main sections of the Bible.\r\n* Recognize the purpose of Scripture in the Christian life.\r\n* Develop a habit of personal Bible study.\r\n\r\nWhat Is the Bible?\r\nThe Bible is a collection of sacred books written over approximately 1,500 years by more than 40 authors from different backgrounds, including kings, prophets, shepherds, fishermen, and scholars.\r\nDespite having many writers, the Bible presents one consistent message: God's love for humanity and His plan to save people from sin through Jesus Christ.\r\nThe word "Bible" comes from a Greek word meaning "books." Although it contains many books, it tells one unified story of creation, redemption, and restoration.\r\n\r\nThe Structure of the Bible\r\nThe Bible is divided into two main sections:\r\n1. Old Testament\r\nThe Old Testament contains 39 books and focuses on:\r\n* Creation of the world\r\n* The history of God's people\r\n* God's laws and commandments\r\n* Prophecies concerning the coming Messiah\r\n* Lessons from the lives of faithful men and women\r\nExamples include Genesis, Exodus, Psalms, Proverbs, Isaiah, and Daniel.\r\n2. New Testament\r\nThe New Testament contains 27 books and focuses on:\r\n* The life and ministry of Jesus Christ\r\n* His death and resurrection\r\n* The growth of the Christian church\r\n* Instructions for Christian living\r\n* Prophecies about the future\r\nExamples include Matthew, Mark, Luke, John, Acts, Romans, and Revelation.\r\nTogether, the Old and New Testaments reveal God's plan of salvation.\r\n\r\nThe Inspiration of the Bible\r\nChristians believe that God inspired the writers of Scripture through the Holy Spirit.\r\nKey Bible Verse\r\n2 Timothy 3:16-17\r\n"All Scripture is given by inspiration of God and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness."\r\nThis means that God guided the writers so that the message they recorded accurately communicates His truth.\r\nAlthough the writers used their own language, culture, and experiences, the Holy Spirit directed them to communicate God's message faithfully.\r\n\r\nWhy Can We Trust the Bible?\r\nChristians trust the Bible because:\r\nHistorical Reliability\r\nMany events, places, and people mentioned in the Bible have been confirmed through historical records and archaeological discoveries.\r\nConsistent Message\r\nAlthough written by many authors over many centuries, the Bible presents a consistent message about God, sin, salvation, and eternal life.\r\nFulfilled Prophecy\r\nThe Bible contains numerous prophecies that were fulfilled, especially concerning the life and ministry of Jesus Christ.\r\nTransforming Power\r\nMillions of people throughout history have experienced life transformation through studying and applying biblical teachings.\r\n\r\nThe Purpose of the Bible\r\nThe Bible serves several important purposes:\r\nTo Reveal God\r\nThe Bible teaches us about God's character, love, justice, mercy, and faithfulness.\r\nTo Teach Truth\r\nIt provides guidance for understanding right and wrong and helps believers make wise decisions.\r\nTo Lead People to Salvation\r\nThe Bible points people to Jesus Christ as the Savior of the world.\r\nTo Strengthen Faith\r\nRegular Bible study helps believers grow spiritually and deepen their relationship with God.\r\nTo Prepare Believers for Service\r\nScripture equips Christians to serve God and others effectively.\r\n\r\nHow to Study the Bible\r\nStudying the Bible should be a regular part of every Christian's life.\r\nPray Before Reading\r\nAsk God for wisdom and understanding.\r\nRead Carefully\r\nPay attention to the meaning of the text and its context.\r\nCompare Scripture with Scripture\r\nUse other Bible passages to help understand difficult verses.\r\nApply What You Learn\r\nThe goal of Bible study is not only knowledge but also spiritual growth and obedience.\r\nStudy Regularly\r\nConsistent study strengthens faith and spiritual maturity.\r\n\r\nBenefits of Bible Study\r\nWhen believers study the Bible regularly, they:\r\n* Grow closer to God.\r\n* Gain wisdom for daily life.\r\n* Strengthen their faith.\r\n* Find comfort during difficulties.\r\n* Learn God's will.\r\n* Develop Christian character.\r\n* Become better witnesses for Christ.\r\n\r\nKey Memory Verse\r\nPsalm 119:105\r\n"Your word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path."\r\nThis verse teaches that God's Word guides believers in making decisions and living according to His will.\r\n\r\nLesson Summary\r\nThe Bible is God's inspired Word and the foundation of Christian faith. It reveals God's character, teaches truth, guides daily living, and leads people to salvation through Jesus Christ. By studying Scripture regularly, believers grow spiritually and develop a closer relationship with God. The Bible remains the ultimate authority for faith, doctrine, and Christian living.\r\n\r\nDiscussion Questions\r\n1. Why is the Bible important to Christians?\r\n2. What are the two main divisions of the Bible?\r\n3. What does it mean that the Bible is inspired by God?\r\n4. How can the Bible help us in our daily lives?\r\n5. What steps can you take to develop a regular Bible study habit?	\N	0	50	\N	NOT_STARTED	\N	\N	1	1
2	2026-08-06 00:30:58.051589	2026-08-06 00:31:53.059449	\N	\N	\N	t	2026-08-06 00:31:43.466442	100	Discover the nature and work of the Godhead, including the love of the Father, the saving ministry of Jesus Christ, and the guidance of the Holy Spirit.	\N	/Users/macbook/uploads/ec4839e9-0e22-4188-9148-e22954af9f55_genzura1.jpeg	300	2026-08-05	1	God the Father, Jesus Christ, and the Holy Spirit	3	Lesson 2: The Bible – God's Word and Authority\r\nIntroduction\r\nThe Bible is the foundation of the Christian faith. It reveals who God is, explains His plan for humanity, teaches us how to live, and provides guidance for every aspect of life. Christians believe that the Bible is not merely a collection of human writings but the inspired Word of God given through human authors under the guidance of the Holy Spirit.\r\nStudying the Bible helps us understand God's character, His love for humanity, and His plan of salvation through Jesus Christ. It is the primary source of truth and the standard by which Christians evaluate beliefs and practices.\r\n\r\nLearning Objectives\r\nBy the end of this lesson, learners should be able to:\r\n* Understand what the Bible is and why it is important.\r\n* Explain how the Bible was inspired by God.\r\n* Identify the two main sections of the Bible.\r\n* Recognize the purpose of Scripture in the Christian life.\r\n* Develop a habit of personal Bible study.\r\n\r\nWhat Is the Bible?\r\nThe Bible is a collection of sacred books written over approximately 1,500 years by more than 40 authors from different backgrounds, including kings, prophets, shepherds, fishermen, and scholars.\r\nDespite having many writers, the Bible presents one consistent message: God's love for humanity and His plan to save people from sin through Jesus Christ.\r\nThe word "Bible" comes from a Greek word meaning "books." Although it contains many books, it tells one unified story of creation, redemption, and restoration.\r\n\r\nThe Structure of the Bible\r\nThe Bible is divided into two main sections:\r\n1. Old Testament\r\nThe Old Testament contains 39 books and focuses on:\r\n* Creation of the world\r\n* The history of God's people\r\n* God's laws and commandments\r\n* Prophecies concerning the coming Messiah\r\n* Lessons from the lives of faithful men and women\r\nExamples include Genesis, Exodus, Psalms, Proverbs, Isaiah, and Daniel.\r\n2. New Testament\r\nThe New Testament contains 27 books and focuses on:\r\n* The life and ministry of Jesus Christ\r\n* His death and resurrection\r\n* The growth of the Christian church\r\n* Instructions for Christian living\r\n* Prophecies about the future\r\nExamples include Matthew, Mark, Luke, John, Acts, Romans, and Revelation.\r\nTogether, the Old and New Testaments reveal God's plan of salvation.\r\n\r\nThe Inspiration of the Bible\r\nChristians believe that God inspired the writers of Scripture through the Holy Spirit.\r\nKey Bible Verse\r\n2 Timothy 3:16-17\r\n"All Scripture is given by inspiration of God and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness."\r\nThis means that God guided the writers so that the message they recorded accurately communicates His truth.\r\nAlthough the writers used their own language, culture, and experiences, the Holy Spirit directed them to communicate God's message faithfully.\r\n\r\nWhy Can We Trust the Bible?\r\nChristians trust the Bible because:\r\nHistorical Reliability\r\nMany events, places, and people mentioned in the Bible have been confirmed through historical records and archaeological discoveries.\r\nConsistent Message\r\nAlthough written by many authors over many centuries, the Bible presents a consistent message about God, sin, salvation, and eternal life.\r\nFulfilled Prophecy\r\nThe Bible contains numerous prophecies that were fulfilled, especially concerning the life and ministry of Jesus Christ.\r\nTransforming Power\r\nMillions of people throughout history have experienced life transformation through studying and applying biblical teachings.\r\n\r\nThe Purpose of the Bible\r\nThe Bible serves several important purposes:\r\nTo Reveal God\r\nThe Bible teaches us about God's character, love, justice, mercy, and faithfulness.\r\nTo Teach Truth\r\nIt provides guidance for understanding right and wrong and helps believers make wise decisions.\r\nTo Lead People to Salvation\r\nThe Bible points people to Jesus Christ as the Savior of the world.\r\nTo Strengthen Faith\r\nRegular Bible study helps believers grow spiritually and deepen their relationship with God.\r\nTo Prepare Believers for Service\r\nScripture equips Christians to serve God and others effectively.\r\n\r\nHow to Study the Bible\r\nStudying the Bible should be a regular part of every Christian's life.\r\nPray Before Reading\r\nAsk God for wisdom and understanding.\r\nRead Carefully\r\nPay attention to the meaning of the text and its context.\r\nCompare Scripture with Scripture\r\nUse other Bible passages to help understand difficult verses.\r\nApply What You Learn\r\nThe goal of Bible study is not only knowledge but also spiritual growth and obedience.\r\nStudy Regularly\r\nConsistent study strengthens faith and spiritual maturity.\r\n\r\nBenefits of Bible Study\r\nWhen believers study the Bible regularly, they:\r\n* Grow closer to God.\r\n* Gain wisdom for daily life.\r\n* Strengthen their faith.\r\n* Find comfort during difficulties.\r\n* Learn God's will.\r\n* Develop Christian character.\r\n* Become better witnesses for Christ.\r\n\r\nKey Memory Verse\r\nPsalm 119:105\r\n"Your word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path."\r\nThis verse teaches that God's Word guides believers in making decisions and living according to His will.\r\n\r\nLesson Summary\r\nThe Bible is God's inspired Word and the foundation of Christian faith. It reveals God's character, teaches truth, guides daily living, and leads people to salvation through Jesus Christ. By studying Scripture regularly, believers grow spiritually and develop a closer relationship with God. The Bible remains the ultimate authority for faith, doctrine, and Christian living.\r\n\r\nDiscussion Questions\r\n1. Why is the Bible important to Christians?\r\n2. What are the two main divisions of the Bible?\r\n3. What does it mean that the Bible is inspired by God?\r\n4. How can the Bible help us in our daily lives?\r\n5. What steps can you take to develop a regular Bible study habit?	\N	100	70	2026-08-06 00:31:28.712692	COMPLETED	\N	\N	1	1
